{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>ויעמידם</b> — its meaning is that they never change, for they are not composed of the four elements." "<b>חק נתן ולא יעבור</b> — the decree is one of them, or the decree shall not cease. And the reason: that Saturn completes the revolution of its sphere [in] fifty-nine years, and so for each one an everlasting decree. And the prophet said: If these ordinances depart (Jeremiah 31:35). Now he begins to mention the lower world, and he begins to mention the sea-monsters that are in the sea, for the earth and the waters are one sphere by absolute proofs, and behold sea-monsters that are alive, and depths that are not alive, and behold he mentioned those that are beneath the inhabited earth, and afterward he mentioned —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:07.886601440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}